    "note_verbatim": "Rene Tavernier edited Confluences, a journal of literature and art, from 1941 to 1947. Contributor to several French periodicals, including Arts, Preuves, Carrefour and Franc-Tireur. K.rishnanath reviews books regularly for Thought. Contributions are invited and will be paid for. A stamped addressed envelope must be enclosed for the return of unaccepted manuscripts THE ARYAN PATH A HIGH-CLASS INTERNATIONAL NON-POLITICAL AND NON-SECTARIAN JOURNAL Outstanding Features of The Journal EDITORIALS discuss with unprejudiced frankness the vital problems of the day from the universal and spiritual point of view. ARTICLES authoritative, stimulating and of high intellectual tone; deal with various phases of Philosophy, Religion, Art and Science of all peoplesancient and modern. REVIEWS of the latest books and publications from all countries; a guide to world literature each month. ENDS & SAYINGS distinctive feature of the journal, a section of short notes and topical comments of interest to the thoughtful reader. ANNUAL SUBSCRIPTION-In India Rs. 6 / -; in Europe 12 sh,; in U.S.A. $3.00 Single copy As. 12; Is. 6d.; 35 cents respectively A sample copy will be sent on receipt Of postage stamps of 12 annas Managerial Office: No. 1 North Public Square Road, BANGALORE-4 (INDIA).",
    "note_printed_page": 72,
    "nationality_evidence": null,
